# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — The First Page
# A small playable opening and a map of the starter project.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_prologue
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
@position desk_left 0.28 0.96

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
{{BG_START}}{{BG_TRANSITION}}[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[textspeed 26]
[autodelay 1500]
[set visit_count 0]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
[show lavender left idle]
[wait 250]

narrator: A white page. A familiar pencil drawing.
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: There you are. I was beginning to think this project would stay blank forever.
Lavender: I'm Lavender. This studio—and the story inside it—belongs to you now.
[show lavender left happy]
Lavender: We only need one honest first line. The second line is always easier.

> Write the first line with Lavender -> write_first_line
> Open Lavender’s complete JVN workshop -> route_tutorial
> Preview a JES scene -> open_jes
> Explore a branching story example -> route_branch

@label write_first_line
[inc visit_count]
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Good. Let's keep it simple: what should a new project promise?
> A place to tell a story -> promise_story
> A place to experiment -> promise_experiment
> A project I can actually finish -> promise_finish

@label promise_story
[set project_promise story]
narrator: {i}A place to tell a story.{/i}
[jump promise_kept]

@label promise_experiment
[set project_promise experiment]
narrator: {i}A place to experiment.{/i}
[jump promise_kept]

@label promise_finish
[set project_promise finish]
narrator: {i}A project I can actually finish.{/i}
[jump promise_kept]

@label promise_kept
[show lavender left happy]
Lavender: That's a real beginning. The variable {b}project_promise{/b} now remembers your choice.
Lavender: Open this file beside the running game. Change a line, add a choice, and run it again.
> Explore JVN one feature at a time -> route_tutorial
> See the multi-file story route -> route_branch
> Visit the JES studio overlay -> open_jes

@label open_jes
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: VNS handles this conversation. JES handles entity scenes, input, and timelines.
Lavender: The next screen is authored in {b}scripts/scenes/studio_tour.jes{/b}. Press Enter to return here.
[jes push {{JES_SCENE_PATH}} label jes_returned with source=starter]

@label jes_returned
[show lavender left happy]
Lavender: Welcome back. That was a real VNS to JES scene transition, not a mock-up.
> Continue to the tutorials -> route_tutorial
> Continue to the branch demo -> route_branch
> Return to the opening choices -> start

@label route_tutorial
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[goto {{TUTORIAL_TARGET}}:start]

@label route_branch
[goto {{BRANCH_TARGET}}:start]
